  Method: every leg carries THREE flows at once -- the subject group, a control group
  that was never joined and must NOT arrive, and an instrument control (routed ICMP
  unicast 10.38.22.40 -> 10.38.22.65) that must always arrive. The instrument control
  arrived at its full count in every one of the 9 counted legs, so every zero in this
  log is a measurement and not a dead capture. It also arrives with Ethernet source
  88:9d:98:df:26:02 = swi_a's MAC, which is itself the proof that the two-router path is
  real: the frame was routed by the DUT, crossed the trunk, and was routed again by the
  partner before reaching eth4. One foreign host, 10.38.22.41 / 00:0c:25:2a:a5:53, lives
  on the eth3 (source) segment; every count below is taken on eth4 and attributed by
  source address AND by both MACs, so its traffic cannot be mistaken for a measurement.

