  One command fixed it:

swi_a(config-if)#ip igmp
swi_a#show ip igmp interface vlan48
 IGMP Enabled, Active, Querier, Version 3 (default)
swi_a#show ip pim sparse-mode local-members
vlan48:
  (*, 239.1.1.1) : Include                                            <-- PIM sees it now

  => STEP 2 PASS as a measurement, and it is the step that produced finding F-13: on
     this build a receiver interface needs BOTH `ip pim sparse-mode` and an explicit
     `ip igmp`. Until `ip igmp` is given, `show ip igmp groups` lists the group with a
     live expiry timer -- learned by IGMP SNOOPING, which is on by default and does not
     feed PIM -- while `show ip pim sparse-mode local-members` is empty and the dataplane
     forwards nothing. Two read-backs disagree at the same instant and the dataplane
     follows the second. A related cosmetic defect is visible above and is recorded as
     O-21: `show ip igmp groups` prints `Last Reporter 0.0.0.0` even though the report
     on the wire carries a correct on-subnet source (10.38.22.70, confirmed by capture),
     both before and after `ip igmp` was enabled.

